      <title>Palma airport set for €621.6M revamp, including runways, terminals, boarding bridges and parking</title>
      <link>https://www.majorcadailybulletin.com/holiday/airport/2026/02/25/140503/palma-airport-set-for-6216m-revamp-including-runways-terminals-boarding-bridges-and-parking.html</link>
      <description>Spain’s airport operator AENA has announced plans to invest €621.6 million in Palma de Mallorca airport between 2027 and 2031, representing a 46.7% increase on the €424 million allocated for the previous five-year period. The funds will be directed towards upgrading runways, taxiways, and parking facilities at the island’s busiest airport.</description>
